For ELMo's prize at NAACL 2018: they had announced the set of prize winners ahead of time but not the top prize winner. However, everyone knew that ELMo would win the top prize. I was there with Nick Dingwall, my coauthor on a static vectors paper, and, sitting together in the awards session, we agreed it was lucky we got the paper accepted that year, since everything was clearly going to be contextual from then on.
